WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.080
A student struggling in precalculus usually isn't struggling with precalculus.

00:04.080 --> 00:09.600
They're carrying something from Algebra 2 that never got fixed, and every new topic lands on top of it.

00:10.160 --> 00:14.320
Homework help can't see that. It walks your student through tonight's assignment,

00:14.320 --> 00:18.080
and next week the same thing happens again, because the real problem was never addressed.

00:18.640 --> 00:23.280
I start with the gap. The first sessions find it, the plan fixes it first,

00:23.280 --> 00:25.840
and that's when the new material finally starts to stick.

00:26.480 --> 00:31.360
This isn't only for students who are behind. Some of my students are ahead and want to stay there.

00:31.840 --> 00:36.000
The plan comes from where your student actually is, not where the class is.

00:37.040 --> 00:44.640
I cover Algebra 1 through AP Calculus, Statistics, Multivariable, Linear Algebra, IB Math, and most college mathematics.

00:45.280 --> 00:50.400
Every month you get a written report on where things stand, so you always know whether it's working.

00:51.360 --> 00:56.240
Whether your student is getting ahead, bringing a grade up, or just needs tutoring that adapts to them,

00:56.240 --> 01:00.300
the first call is free, and you get the plan in writing before we start.
